# EasyModelePdf language file - en_US
Module185165Name=EasyModelePdf
Module185165Desc=Install your custom PDF document models (pdf_*.modules.php) with a simple drag & drop

EmpSetup=EasyModelePdf setup
EmpSetupIntro=Drop your custom PDF model files (pdf_xxx.modules.php). The module automatically detects the target object (order, invoice, proposal...), checks that the class name matches the file name, then installs the model. It then shows up in the native document model list of the related object.
EmpDropZoneText=Drag & drop your pdf_xxx.modules.php files here, or click to browse
EmpDropZoneHint=Multiple files accepted. An already installed file gets updated.
EmpNoModelYet=No model installed yet. Drop a first file above.
EmpDeployed=Deployed
EmpRedeploy=Redeploy all models
EmpRedeployed=%s model(s) redeployed into the module tree
EmpFileInstalled=Model %s installed (object: %s)
EmpFileUpdated=Model %s updated (object: %s)
EmpFileDeleted=Model %s deleted
EmpConfirmDelete=Permanently delete model %s (stored file + deployed file)?

EmpErrBadFileName=%s: file name must look like pdf_name.modules.php
EmpErrCannotRead=%s: unreadable file
EmpErrNoClass=%s: no PHP class found in file
EmpErrSyntax=%s: PHP syntax error, file rejected: %s
EmpErrClassMismatch=%s: the class must be named "%s" (Dolibarr rule: class = file name). Found class(es): %s
EmpErrUnsupportedParent=%s: unsupported parent class "%s". Supported parent classes: %s
EmpErrUpload=%s: error while uploading file
EmpErrTooBig=%s: file too big (max 4 MB)
EmpErrMkdir=Cannot create directory %s
EmpErrCopy=Cannot write file %s
EmpErrDelete=Cannot delete %s
EmpWarnNotWritable=The module directory (%s) is not writable by the web server: models cannot be deployed. Fix permissions.
EmpCarriedModels=Installed models
EmpAvailableModels=Available models to download (%s)
EmpAvailableIntro=PDF models shipped by Dolibarr and the other enabled modules. Download one as a starting point, rename the file AND the class (pdf_mymodel), customize it, then drop it above.
EmpOrigin=Origin
EmpConfirmInUse=WARNING: %s object(s) of type "%s" still use this model. Their PDF cannot be regenerated until another model is assigned to them.
EmpConfirmIsDefault=WARNING: this is the default model for "%s". After deletion no default model will be set.
